Where local regulations are inconsistent with rules, the relevant authority shall rule in accordance with the following limits of authority:
(1) Where new general provisions enacted by the same authority are inconsistent with old special provisions, the enacting authority shall rule;
(2) Where provisions of a local regulation are inconsistent with those of a departmental rule on the same matter and it cannot be determined which to apply, the State Council shall provide its opinion; if the State Council considers that the local regulation shall apply, it shall decide that the provisions of the local regulation shall apply in that locality; if it considers that the departmental rule shall apply, it shall request the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress to rule;
(3) Where provisions of departmental rules are inconsistent among themselves or with those of local government rules on the same matter, the State Council shall rule.
Where a regulation enacted under authorization is inconsistent with the provisions of a law and it cannot be determined which to apply, the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress shall rule.

Where any of the following circumstances exists in a law, administrative regulation, local regulation, autonomous regulation, separate regulation, or rule, the relevant authority shall amend or annul it in accordance with the limits of authority prescribed in Article 108 of this Law:
(1) it exceeds the limits of authority;
(2) a lower-level rule violates the provisions of a higher-level rule;
(3) provisions of rules on the same matter are inconsistent and, after a ruling, the provisions of one party shall be amended or annulled;
(4) provisions of a rule are deemed inappropriate and shall be amended or annulled;
(5) it violates statutory procedures.

The limits of authority for amending or annulling laws, administrative regulations, local regulations, autonomous regulations, separate regulations, and rules are as follows:
(1) The National People's Congress has the power to amend or annul any inappropriate law enacted by its Standing Committee, and to annul any autonomous regulation or separate regulation approved by its Standing Committee that violates the Constitution or the provisions of Paragraph 2 of Article 85 of this Law;
(2) The Standing Committee of the National People's Congress has the power to annul any administrative regulation that contravenes the Constitution or a law, to annul any local regulation that contravenes the Constitution, a law, or an administrative regulation, and to annul any autonomous regulation or separate regulation approved by the Standing Committee of the People's Congress of a province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the Central Government that violates the Constitution or the provisions of Paragraph 2 of Article 85 of this Law;
(3) The State Council has the power to amend or annul any inappropriate departmental rule or local government rule;
(4) The People's Congress of a province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the Central Government has the power to amend or annul any inappropriate local regulation enacted or approved by its Standing Committee;
(5) The Standing Committee of a local People's Congress has the power to annul any inappropriate rule enacted by the people's government at the corresponding level;
(6) The people's government of a province or autonomous region has the power to amend or annul any inappropriate rule enacted by the people's government at the next lower level;
(7) The authorizing authority has the power to annul any regulation enacted by the authorized authority that exceeds the scope of authorization or violates the purpose of authorization, and may, when necessary, revoke the authorization.

Administrative regulations, local regulations, autonomous regulations, separate regulations, and rules shall, within thirty days of their promulgation, be submitted to the relevant authority for archival filing in accordance with the following provisions:
(1) Administrative regulations shall be filed with the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress for archival filing;
(2) Local regulations enacted by the People's Congress or its Standing Committee of a province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the Central Government shall be filed with the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress and the State Council for archival filing; local regulations enacted by the People's Congress or its Standing Committee of a city divided into districts or an autonomous prefecture shall be filed by the Standing Committee of the People's Congress of the province or autonomous region with the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress and the State Council for archival filing;
(3) Autonomous regulations and separate regulations enacted by the People's Congress of an autonomous prefecture or autonomous county shall be filed by the Standing Committee of the People's Congress of the province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the Central Government with the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress and the State Council for archival filing; when an autonomous regulation or separate regulation is submitted for archival filing, an explanation of the adaptive provisions made for laws, administrative regulations, and local regulations shall be provided;
(4) Departmental rules and local government rules shall be filed with the State Council for archival filing; a local government rule shall also be filed with the Standing Committee of the People's Congress at the corresponding level for archival filing; a rule enacted by the people's government of a city divided into districts or an autonomous prefecture shall also be filed with the Standing Committee of the People's Congress and the people's government of the province or autonomous region for archival filing;
(5) A regulation enacted under authorization shall be filed with the authority specified in the authorization decision for archival filing; when the regulations of a special economic zone, the Pudong New Area regulations, or the Hainan Free Trade Port regulations are submitted for archival filing, an explanation of the adaptive provisions shall be provided.
